{"author":{"id":"6d85cf2fcebaeefd8c5c528f2d5f5f98f26ce3275422d0dc5f7c0fd596f9f59f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791729863,"nonce":"PsD3PjaSc+YXFQfGpeayhnVgf2c=","title":"line-clamp","message":"line-clamp (and -webkit-line-clamp) on a block container holds the text under it to that many lines. Two parts. In layout, Tree::sync_line_clamps, run before each compute, caps each text node's max height under a clamped container at lines times its line pitch (font size times line height), and lets go when the clamp is taken away or the text moves out; a container with a clamp of its own clamps what it holds. In paint, a text of more lines than the clamp is re-shaped as the longest start of the text with an ellipsis after it that fits that many lines, found by halving. The other half of the idiom, display: -webkit-box and -webkit-box-orient, is not needed: the property is read on any container. Limits: the pitch is the CSS line height, so a line box taller for a fallback font is not counted; a clamp over text in an inline flow (spans, links) is the host's.","files":null}]}